# Optional. Raises the GitHub API rate limit from 60 to 5000 requests per hour.
# The site works without it: every GitHub call falls back to a link when it fails.
# Set it in production, where the egress IP is shared and 60/hour can run out.
#
# Create a fine-grained token with NO permissions:
#   Settings > Developer settings > Personal access tokens > Fine-grained tokens
#   Repository access: Public Repositories (read-only)
#   Permissions: leave empty. The repo is public, so no permission is needed.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
